# Satoru's ruling (2024-04-12): Bot2's Aven Interrupter exiles Bot1's Llanowar Elves and plots it, and on turn 5 Bot1 casts it
# from exile without paying its mana cost, but Aven's static ability makes it cost {2} more (CR 601.2f, 118.9d). Mana was
# spent to cast it (CR 601.2h), though not on its mana cost, so Satoru does not trigger as it enters: Bot1's hand stays the
# three Islands of the first check (a draw would make it four).

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Sapphire
Mox Jet
Mox Emerald
Mox Ruby
Satoru, the Infiltrator
Llanowar Elves
Island x12

[Bot2 Deck]
Mox Pearl x3
Aven Interrupter
Island x16

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Satoru, the Infiltrator.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Llanowar Elves.Cast
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Aven Interrupter.Cast
[T5 Bot1.Main1]
? Bot1.Hand.Count = 3
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Exile.Llanowar Elves.Cast
Bot1.Choose(Close mana window)
? Bot1.Mana =
[T5 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot1.Hand.Count = 3
Bot1.Battlefield.Llanowar Elves.Power = 1
